{
  "requirement": "`matches` holds the results found. `complete` is true when the search exhausted the scope. Reaching the exact limit is compatible with a complete result if no further match exists.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct SearchResults<T> {\n    pub matches: Vec<T>,\n    pub complete: bool,\n}\n\nimpl<T> SearchResults<T> {\n    pub fn new(matches: Vec<T>, complete: bool) -> Self;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.search.SearchResults`.\n\n**`matches` holds the results found.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/search.rs#fn[callers_can_construct_complete_and_partial_search_results]` builds results through `SearchResults::new` with a `TextMatch` and a `StructuralMatch`. It asserts the stored matches (path, line, excerpt, node) and the `complete` flag.\n- `sources/tests.rs#fn[completeness_is_false_only_when_a_match_is_omitted_and_errors_propagate]` asserts `matches.len()` against the expected count.\n\n**`complete` is true when the scope was exhausted, and reaching the exact limit is still complete.**\n- That same text-search test runs these `(limit, count, complete)` cases: `(None,2,true)`, `(Some(2),2,true)`, `(Some(1),1,false)` and `(Some(0),0,false)`. It also runs a case with no match and `limit` 0, which is complete with empty matches.\n- `sources/tests.rs#fn[structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope]` covers the structural case. `(None,1,true)`, `(Some(1),1,true)` (the limit is reached but nothing further exists) and `(Some(0),0,false)` are all asserted.\n- Both tests use the default provider functions `search_text_with` and `search_structure_with`. Those functions build `SearchResults` and set `complete` to false only when a further match is found at the limit.\n\n**Shape of the type.**\n- `#[non_exhaustive]` is checked by the `compile_fail,E0639` doctest on `public.rs#struct[SearchResults]`. It tries struct-literal construction from outside the crate.\n- The `new` constructor is exercised in the `new` test above.\n- `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the export inventory against the appendix.\n\nThe tests assert the outcomes. I found no gap and no marking gap.",
